@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/index.ts` already holds `resolvePointer` and `applyPatch`, which use `Object.hasOwn` for own-member checks and return new values. See proposal.md for motivation.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** a pure, recursive implementation of the RFC 7386 pseudocode; consistent with `applyPatch` (no mutation, no shared structure).
+
+**Non-Goals:** generating merge patches from two documents; validating that inputs are JSON.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Always build new values.** Recurse into a fresh object, copying target members and cloning patch values, instead of mutating a clone. Alternative: deep-clone the target first and mutate it; rejected as it clones twice.
+- **Plain-object test:** a value is an object if it is non-null, `typeof "object"` and not an array.
+- **Own members only, safe assignment.** Use `Object.keys` / `Object.hasOwn`, and write results with `Object.defineProperty` (enumerable, writable, configurable) so a `__proto__` key becomes an own property rather than setting the prototype.
+- **Nested patch values:** a patch object merged onto a missing/non-object target goes through the same recursion with `{}`, which drops nested nulls as RFC 7386 requires; arrays and scalars are deep-cloned.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Result differs from a naive implementation for `{"a":{"b":null}}` on `{}`: gives `{"a":{}}`] → This is the RFC behavior and is covered by a test.
